text=f'''# D04 starboard-aft receiving and court loops

The north and south receiving-street ends now connect to enclosed perimeter loops serving all nine broad courts through full-size private staff fittings. Two normal staff portals control receiving access. The 0.75 m eastern court stays sealed with no entry or work-reach acceptance. Original public receiving, commons and stock/returns approaches remain shared; no dedicated lower vertical or complete clean/used network is claimed.

The package adds {p['new_floor_m2']:.2f} m² of missing perimeter floor, with no duplicated original public or commons floor and no overlap of the protected D03 Staff Administration footprint. No lower-room columns or ceiling cuts are added. Ledger/ring framing remains within the D04 floor thickness, with 108 exact named court-side and 40 exact end-floor contacts. Cantilever sizing, original floor capacity and primary engineering remain held.

Focused checks pass: {g['checks']:,} geometry checks, {g['exact_retained_original_meshes']:,} exact surrounding meshes in the affected/protected scope, 30 exact runtime preimages, 440 actual original-controller gate poses and 135 worker capsule samples. The programme audit passes {vol['conservative_part_programme_volume_checks']:,} conservative checks across 161 programmes without unexplained conflicts. The connected original-player test passes {conn['checks']} checks over {len(conn['original_player_controller_legs'])} walking legs, from one original receiving fixture seed through both loops and back to the original public receiving/commons interfaces. There are no route teleports. All private visits are explicit temporary test fixtures; production permission/provider stays absent and the gates default closed.

All 4,390 prior managed native/export files remain byte-identical, including the approved connected port-central commons. The two new editable native candidates have byte-identical fresh repeat exports. All 55 copied gate mesh payloads retain vertices, faces, UVs, packed texture bytes, roughness and material links. Ten original planter/soil/foliage meshes move rigidly within two short courts; longer-court gates use existing gaps. Twenty bounded clip successors retain outside triangles and original UVs. Inactive geometry was independently retained at `{p['independently_retained_inactive_geometry_commit']}` before integration.

Four partial native diagnostic views include the original home, commons, floor and roof context. They are dark/grainy views with fill, with no ordinary-game/full-ship/CRT/hardware/final visual acceptance. The narrow-court screen is obscured by the new route enclosure in its diagnostic image; the unchanged-source geometry check establishes its preservation.

Original room IDs, 120 home allocations/150 reserved rests, public routes, D03 Uniforms & Lockers ceiling, D05 datums and the approved port-central commons remain intact. Engineering, private consent/vacancy/provider, refill/save/inventory/operational returns, loaded-cart vertical, habitat/biology, final visuals and all eight groups remain unfinished. Two historical unpublished native byte versions remain unavailable. The earlier narrow starboard-forward court also remains sealed without entry/work-reach acceptance.
'''
